# Build context is the repo root (services/*/Dockerfile need libs/), so the
# context includes everything by default — including twelve ZIP_* archive
# directories and the local virtualenv. Excluding them here is the difference
# between a context measured in kilobytes and one that ships the whole design
# history to the daemon on every build. Sprint 2 Task 2.6.

# Architecture archives and contracts: documentation, never imported at runtime.
ZIP_*/
*.zip

.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. .env.example stays out too — it is
# documentation, and the values are placeholders.
.env
.env.*

# Test code is not shipped — except the recorded fixtures the connector's fetch
# stub actually reads at runtime (INPUTS_NEEDED.md item 1). Both patterns are
# needed: the first is repo-root `tests/`, the second is each service's own.
tests/
services/*/tests/
!services/*/tests/fixtures/

admin-dashboard/node_modules/
